This repository is a throughline *source*: a requirements graph, not a program. It
expresses the SOLID principles of object-oriented design as a grounded IDD graph so
consuming projects can compose it with throughline.

The wording of every item is original to this repository. No text is reproduced from
any publication. The principles themselves are the work of their authors: the
Single Responsibility, Open-Closed (as named), Interface Segregation and Dependency
Inversion principles were formulated and collected by Robert C. Martin; the
Open-Closed principle was first stated by Bertrand Meyer; the Liskov Substitution
principle is Barbara Liskov's, with its behavioural formulation by Liskov and Jeannette
Wing; the acronym SOLID was coined by Michael Feathers. Each item cites, in
`attrs.source_ref`, the publication and chapter it is drawn from, so a reader can go
to the authoritative statement. Those publications remain the copyright of their
authors and publishers and are not licensed by this repository.
